# Sanity CMS (required for blog + Studio)
# Find these in https://www.sanity.io/manage after creating a project.
PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID=your_project_id_here
PUBLIC_SANITY_DATASET=production

# Optional: only needed for draft preview or private datasets.
# SANITY_API_READ_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloudflare Workers (Git deploy)
#
# There are TWO places for env vars — both matter:
#
# 1. BUILD variables (Settings → Builds → Build variables)
#    Used during `npm run build`. Without these, blog HTML is generated
#    without Sanity content and /admin is not registered.
#
# 2. RUNTIME variables (Settings → Variables and Secrets, or wrangler.jsonc `vars`)
#    Used when the Worker serves requests (e.g. /admin Studio).
#
# This repo also commits sanity.project.json as a public fallback so builds
# work even if build variables are missing. Override with PUBLIC_* env vars if needed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local setup
# 1. Copy this file:  cp .env.example .env
# 2. Paste your Sanity project ID and dataset name.
# 3. Run: npm run dev
# 4. Open the CMS at http://localhost:4321/admin
# 5. In Sanity Manage, add http://localhost:4321 to CORS origins (authenticated requests).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
